{"name":"Silver Lining","hex":"#b8b1a5","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"silver lining","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A favorable aspect or prospect of a mostly unfavorable event or situation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silver_lining"}],"entries":[{"title":"Silver lining (idiom)","blocks":[{"text":"A silver lining is a metaphor for optimism in vernacular English, which means a negative occurrence may have a positive aspect to it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/George_Lansbury_-_cartoon_-_Project_Gutenberg_eText_17653.png/330px-George_Lansbury_-_cartoon_-_Project_Gutenberg_eText_17653.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_lining_(idiom)","wikidata":"Q7516553"},{"title":"Silver Lining (Bonnie Raitt album)","blocks":[{"text":"Silver Lining is the fourteenth studio album by Bonnie Raitt, released in 2002 on Capitol Records.\nThe album peaked at No. 13 on the US Billboard 200.\nSilver Lining has also been certified Gold in the US by the RIAA."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5e/Bonnie_Raitt_-_Silver_Lining.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_Lining_(Bonnie_Raitt_album)","wikidata":"Q2334273"},{"title":"Silver","blocks":[{"text":"Silver is a chemical element; it has symbol Ag and atomic number 47. A soft, white, lustrous transition metal, it exhibits the highest electrical conductivity, thermal conductivity and reflectivity of any metal. Silver is found in the Earth's crust in the pure, free elemental form, as an alloy with gold (electrum) and other metals, and in minerals such as acanthite, argentite and chlorargyrite. Most silver is recovered as a byproduct of lead–zinc, copper and gold mining and refining."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Silver_